      "description": "tag:jobs.ship.edu,2005:/postings/all_jobs Shippensburg University: All Jobs 2026-08-31T16:25:47-04:00 https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3533 2026-08-31T16:25:47-04:00 2026-08-31T16:25:47-04:00 Custodial Worker 1 M-F 3 pm - 11 pm (Temporary) <div>Join a vibrant and purpose-driven community at <strong>Shippensburg University</strong>, located in the scenic Cumberland Valley and spread across a beautiful 210-acre campus with over 40 buildings. We offer a dynamic academic environment with 45 undergraduates, 22 graduate, and 2 doctoral programs. At Shippensburg, our mission is more than words—we are committed to inclusive collaboration, fostering a strong sense of belonging, and celebrating the achievements that drive positive change in our communities. Be part of a team that values innovation, impact, and shared success.<br><br>Shippensburg University is seeking a <strong>temporary</strong> Custodial Worker 1 to provide comprehensive housekeeping and custodial services across campus facilities. This position is scheduled Monday through Friday, from 3:00 p.m. to 11:00 p.m., and will support the cleanliness and upkeep of academic, administrative, residential, and athletic facilities. This temporary position will be needed through no later than <strong>October 31, 2026</strong>.</div><div><br>The successful candidate will play an important role in maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment for students, employees, and visitors while ensuring campus facilities are consistently maintained to a high standard.</div><div><br>As a member of the Facilities Divisional staff, this position is deemed essential. Essential employees must remain or report to work during partial or full day closings of the University due to hazardous road conditions, emergency circumstances or for other reasons.<br><br></div><div><strong>Key Responsibilities:<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Perform general custodial duties such as:<ul><li>Cleaning furniture, fixtures, lavatories, showers, stairways, windows, carpets, and drinking fountains</li><li>Trash removal and floor care (mopping, vacuuming)</li><li>Seasonal deep cleaning (Fall and Spring)</li></ul></li><li>Operate and inspect manual and powered custodial equipment safely</li><li>Monitor and report maintenance issues or needed repairs in buildings and furniture</li><li>Maintain supply and equipment rooms; request supplies as needed</li><li>Follow all safety protocols and participate in training programs</li><li>Provide support during emergencies and scheduled campus events</li><li>Deliver excellent customer service; respond to complaints and service needs with appropriate measure of courtesy and service.</li><li>Maintain effective verbal and written communication with supervisors and team members</li><li>Report incidents and injuries immediately to the appropriate personnel</li></ul><div><br><strong>The full job description will be provided at the time of the scheduled interview</strong></div> Custodial & Housekeeping Services https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3536 2026-09-02T13:28:15-04:00 2026-09-02T13:28:15-04:00 Building Automation Systems Technician 1 (3:00 p.m. - 11:00 p.m.) <div>Join a vibrant and purpose-driven community at <strong>Shippensburg University</strong>, located in the scenic Cumberland Valley and spread across a beautiful 210-acre campus with over 40 buildings. We offer a dynamic academic environment with 45 undergraduate, 22 graduate, and 2 doctoral programs. At Shippensburg, our mission is more than words—we are committed to inclusive collaboration, fostering a strong sense of belonging, and celebrating the achievements that drive positive change in our communities. Be part of a team that values innovation, impact, and shared success<br><br></div><div><strong>Shippensburg University offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees!</strong></div><ul><li>Effective first day of employment: low-cost medical insurance plus free dental, vision, hearing, and prescription coverage.</li><li>Choose from two generous retirement plans:<br>Alternative Retirement Plan (ARP):5% employee contribution, 9.29% employer contribution, Immediate vesting.</li><li>State Employees’ Retirement System (SERS): 8.25% employee contribution, 2.25% employer contribution + pension calculation, 10-year vesting requirement.</li><li>100% tuition waivers for you and your eligible dependents upon completion of probationary period!</li><li>Generous paid time off, employer-paid life insurance, and so much more!</li></ul><div><br>See full details in link below (for AFSCME employees)</div><div><a href=\"https://www.passhe.edu/hr/benefits/documents/benefit-summaries/pebtf-summary.pdf\"><strong>Full Benefits Summary (PDF)</strong></a><strong><br><br></strong>We’re seeking a skilled Facilities Technician to support the maintenance, operation, repair, and improvement of campus buildings, systems, and infrastructure. This role performs a mix of skilled and semi-skilled work, with a focus on building automation systems (BAS), HVAC, plumbing, and electrical components, while addressing a wide range of facilities-related needs.</div><div><br>As a Facilities Division Employee this position is deemed “essential” and must remain or report to work when classes are delayed or cancelled due to hazardous road or weather conditions, emergency circumstances or for other reasons as determined by operational need.<br><br><strong>This position will be working on an alternative work schedule consisting of a 10-day work cycle followed by four (4) consecutive days off.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br></strong><br><strong>Key Duties &amp; Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Install, program, troubleshoot, calibrate, and maintain <strong>Building Automation Systems (BAS)</strong>, including sensors, actuators, control valves, VFDs, thermostats, dampers, and related controls.</li><li>Monitor system performance, respond to alarms and diagnostics, commission new installations, and document software points and device connections.</li><li>Support HVAC and pneumatic control systems while interpreting schematics, blueprints, wiring diagrams, and control sequences.</li><li>Provide technical support and training to building occupants and staff on BAS operations.</li><li>Perform multi-trade maintenance and repair work across HVAC, electrical, plumbing, carpentry, masonry, and welding disciplines.</li><li>Maintain and repair building infrastructure, including pumps, piping, lighting, motors, ventilation equipment, air compressors, heating systems, doors, partitions, furniture, electrical fixtures, and circuits.</li><li>Conduct preventive maintenance, facility inspections, and corrective repairs to ensure safe and reliable operation of campus facilities.</li><li>Utilize a computerized maintenance management system (CMMS) to manage work orders, document labor and materials, and track maintenance activities.</li><li>Maintain inventory, identify and report unsafe conditions, and recommend equipment replacement or system improvements.</li><li>Participate in emergency response activities, after-hours call coverage, lock changes, and snow/ice removal operations.</li><li>Support campus events through facility setup, teardown, and troubleshooting.</li><li>Obtain Pennsylvania Pesticide Applicator Certification in Swimming Pool Management (Category 24) within 180 days of hire.</li></ul><div><strong>Qualifications:</strong></div><ul><li>Proficiency in at least two trades: plumbing, electrical, HVAC, carpentry, or mechanical systems</li><li>Working knowledge of BAS software and commercial system components</li><li>Ability to diagnose and resolve mechanical/electrical issues using tools and technical documentation</li><li>Familiarity with safety standards, CMMS, and Microsoft Office</li><li>Strong communication skills and teamwork mindset</li><li>Must obtain PA Pesticide Applicator Certification (Category 24 – Swimming Pool Management) within 180 days of hire</li></ul><div><strong><br><br>A full job description will be provided at the time of the scheduled interview.</strong></div> ROC Maintenance & Operations https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3378 2026-03-27T13:53:26-04:00 2026-03-27T13:53:27-04:00 Police Officer <div>Join a vibrant and purpose-driven community at <strong>Shippensburg University</strong>, located in the scenic Cumberland Valley and spread across a beautiful 210-acre campus with over 40 buildings. We offer a dynamic academic environment with 45 undergraduates, 22 graduate, and 2 doctoral programs. At Shippensburg, our mission is more than words—we are committed to inclusive collaboration, fostering a strong sense of belonging, and celebrating the achievements that drive positive change in our communities. Be part of a team that values innovation, impact, and shared success<br><br></div><div><strong>Shippensburg University offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees!</strong></div><ul><li>Effective first day of employment: low-cost medical insurance plus free dental, vision, hearing, and prescription coverage.</li><li>Choose from two generous retirement plans:<ul><li>Alternative Retirement Plan (ARP): 5% employee contribution, 9.29% employer contribution, Immediate vesting.</li><li>State Employees’ Retirement System (SERS): employee may choose between SERS Class A3 with 6.25% employee contribution or SERS Class A4 with 9.3% employee contribution, with a 10-year vesting requirement.</li></ul></li><li>100% tuition waivers for you and your eligible dependents upon completion of probationary period!</li><li>Generous paid time off, employer-paid life insurance, and so much more!</li></ul><div><br></div><div>See full details in link below (for PASSHE Benefits)</div><div><a href=\"https://www.passhe.edu/hr/benefits/documents/benefit-summaries/sshe-summary.pdf\"><strong>Full Benefits Summary (PDF)</strong></a><strong><br><br></strong>Shippensburg University is currently accepting applications for the position of Police Officer. This position will work a permanent shift.<br><br>To enforce applicable policies and laws in university buildings and grounds. To protect the property of the Commonwealth in all buildings and grounds of the University and to exclude disorderly persons from same. To exercise powers of arrest under authority of law or ordinance wherein the University is located. To perform traffic and crowd control duties while enforcing all traffic laws and regulations of the Commonwealth and the University. Investigate traffic accidents, prepare accident reports and follow-up procedures as may be necessary.</div><div><br>To investigate all crimes. To render assistance to those in distress. To provide public service to both residents and visitors to the University. To provide emergency services as may be necessary and/or directed by standing procedures for all types of disorder or disasters.<br><br>To patrol and secure buildings and grounds as may be necessary during the tour of duty. To operate the University Communications System in accordance with existing FCC rules and regulations. To be responsible for the safety, control and use of Commonwealth property assigned to the University Police Department or the University. To cooperate with all other law enforcement agencies requesting assistance and/or information. To assume the duties of acting supervisor in their absence. Possession of basic computer skills necessary to complete reports and enter information into the department Informant system.</div><div><br></div> Public Safety https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3431 2026-05-31T21:53:09-04:00 2026-05-31T21:53:10-04:00 Student Teaching Supervisor <div>The Department of Teacher Education seeks instructors to supervise student teachers. Selected candidates will be added to a team of university supervisors who will be used on an as-needed basis during the fall and spring semesters.<br><br></div><div>As a university supervisor, you will oversee the student teaching experience for assigned students. Primary duties include mentoring, instructional coaching, and collaborating with host teachers. Responsibilities also encompass the writing of evaluations and recommendation letters, responding to emails and phone calls in a timely manner, and the completion of professorial duties. The work requires travel to local schools and the occasional need to attend campus meetings/events. Please see course catalog for course description (ECED 489)- <a href=\"https://catalog.ship.edu/index.php\"><strong>https://catalog.ship.edu/index.php</strong></a></div> Teacher Education https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3463 2026-07-07T11:28:48-04:00 2026-07-07T11:28:48-04:00 Assistant/Associate Professor - Communication, Journalism and Media <div>The Department of Communication, Journalism and Media, an ACEJMC-accredited program, is seeking candidates with broad expertise in <strong>multimedia production, visual media, and generative AI tools</strong>, who can help meet core departmental teaching needs at the undergraduate and graduate levels for the position of Assistant/Associate Professor of Communication, Journalism and Media, effective August 2027.<br> <br> The ideal candidate must have work/practical experience with broadcast media production and/or digital media tools<strong>, and visual storytelling</strong>. The selected candidate will be expected to teach courses such as <strong>Basic Media Production</strong>, <strong>Digital Photography, Media Field Production, Media Studio Production, Documentary Storytelling </strong>and core courses across the curriculum such as media writing and media literacy. The department is seeking a candidate who can also offer new and innovative courses, especially in areas such as emerging media technologies and Generative <strong>AI-assisted mass communication</strong>.<br><br></div><div>Successful candidates must have teaching experience and/or significant professional experience <strong>in one or more of the following areas:</strong> video editing, post-production, <strong>digital photography, social/digital video storytelling, and AI-enhanced media workflows</strong>. Prior teaching and/or research experience in any of these areas is a plus.<br><br></div><div>The anticipated start date is <strong>August 2027</strong>. Shippensburg is a teaching-focused institution, and the teaching load is expected to be 4/4 (four courses per semester), with potential opportunities to teach special topic courses during summer or winter terms for additional compensation. Teaching assignments may include both face-to-face and online courses. Part of the teaching load may include advising student media such as SUTV.</div><div><br>We seek collegial faculty who value and create transformative teaching and learning environments, and who can make positive contributions in service, outreach, and engagement. The successful applicant will exhibit a demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching courses in our curriculum. In addition, we expect the candidate to take an active role in the department by pursuing professional, creative, and/or scholarly activity; developing new curricula; advising students; serving on departmental and university committees; and assisting student media organizations.<br><br>Requirements for the on-campus interview include a presentation of recent research and/or a professional portfolio, a teaching demonstration, and evidence of a commitment to understanding diverse populations. We strive to enhance the diversity of our department and the university community, and encourage applicants who exemplify multi-cultural, multi-disciplinary, and global perspectives.</div> Communication, Journalism and Media https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3511 2026-08-11T08:21:56-04:00 2026-08-11T08:21:57-04:00 PDO Professional Development Coordinator (SCUPA/GFPC 1) <div>Join a vibrant and purpose-driven community at <strong>Shippensburg University</strong>, located in the scenic Cumberland Valley and spread across a beautiful 210-acre campus with over 40 buildings. We offer a dynamic academic environment with 45 undergraduates, 22 graduate, and 2 doctoral programs. At Shippensburg, our mission is more than words—we are committed to inclusive collaboration, fostering a strong sense of belonging, and celebrating the achievements that drive positive change in our communities. Be part of a team that values innovation, impact, and shared success<br><br></div><div><strong>Shippensburg University offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees!</strong></div><ul><li>Effective first day of employment: low-cost medical insurance plus free dental, vision, hearing, and prescription coverage.</li><li>Choose from two generous retirement plans:<br>Alternative Retirement Plan (ARP): 5% employee contribution, 9.29% employer contribution, Immediate vesting.</li><li>State Employees’ Retirement System (SERS): 8.25% employee contribution, 2.25% employer contribution + pension calculation, 10-year vesting requirement.</li><li>Generous paid time off, employer-paid life insurance, and so much more!</li></ul><div><br>See full details in link below.</div><div><a href=\"https://www.passhe.edu/hr/benefits/documents/benefit-summaries/pebtf-summary.pdf\"><strong>Full Benefits Summary (PDF)</strong></a></div><div><br></div><div>The Outreach Coordinator position’s primary purpose is to increase early childhood educators’ understanding about what the PDO is and how their career pathways in ECE can expand and advance with PDO-sponsored tuition and other supports. The overarching PDO goal is to increase the credentials and professional regard of all Pennsylvania EC educators as we build a pipeline of qualified people in this workforce-critical sector.<br><br>This is a grant funded program position for 2 years<br>Summary of Duties</div><ul><li>Manage participant eligibility, enrollment, and ongoing compliance by collecting and verifying required employment, wage, residency, academic, and program documentation.</li><li>Confirm and accurately record participant eligibility through the PD Registry and related online systems.</li><li>Ensure all required enrollment documents, including Commitment Forms and FERPA releases, are complete and properly submitted.</li><li>Support the planning and coordination of professional development events, including scheduling, registration, participant communication, meeting locations, trainer logistics, travel arrangements, and materials.</li><li>Guide Professional Development Organization and grant-funded students through the full Child Development Associate credentialing process.</li><li>Provide individualized advising, coaching, and mentoring related to CDA requirements, competency standards, portfolios, documentation, assessments, and professional writing.</li><li>Review candidate portfolios and supporting documentation for accuracy, completeness, and compliance with CDA Council guidelines.</li><li>Monitor student progress, maintain detailed records, and support timely completion of all credentialing requirements.</li><li>Facilitate workshops and one-on-one support sessions to strengthen reflective practice, accountability, confidence, and professional growth.</li><li>Prepare candidates for CDA verification visits and competency-based assessments.</li><li>Collaborate with instructors, administrators, and field supervisors to support candidate success.</li><li>Remain current on CDA Council policies, credentialing requirements, and early childhood education best practices.</li><li>Provide professional development coordination and CDA guidance to School to Work Round 6 Grant and OCDEL PDO students.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Full job description will be provided at time of interview.<br></strong><br></div> Teacher Education https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3516 2026-08-20T08:12:15-04:00 2026-08-20T08:12:15-04:00 Assistant Strength/Conditioning Coach <div>Join a vibrant and purpose-driven community at <strong>Shippensburg University</strong>, located in the scenic Cumberland Valley and spread across a beautiful 210-acre campus with over 40 buildings. We offer a dynamic academic environment with 45 undergraduate, 22 graduate, and 2 doctoral programs. At Shippensburg, our mission is more than words—we are committed to inclusive collaboration, fostering a strong sense of belonging, and celebrating the achievements that drive positive change in our communities. Be part of a team that values innovation, impact, and shared success.<br><br>This is a .25 FTE 12-month.</div><ul><li>To assist management/hour load of strength/conditioning program.</li><li>Report to the head strength and conditioning coach for specific assignments designated by the head coach.</li><li>Adhere to all rules and regulations mandated by Shippensburg University, the Pennsylvania State Athletic Conference (PSAC), and the National Collegiate Athletic Association (NCAA).</li><li>Maintain required NCAA certification.</li><li>Assist with coordinating, implementing, planning, and managing in-season and out-of-season player development and strength and conditioning including both team and individual programming.</li><li>Attend team strength and conditioning sessions.</li><li>Assist in coordinating and monitoring usage of Raider Athletics Performance Center.</li><li>Assist with overseeing maintenance and cleanliness of Raider Athletics Performance Center including equipment.</li><li>Annually, successfully complete First Aid and Safety and CPR certifications.</li><li>Cooperate with athletic trainers to ensure student-athletes receive proper medical and physical training services.</li><li>Ensure appropriate safety precautions are implemented and followed.</li><li>Assist sports information staff with publicity efforts.</li><li>Attend appropriate athletics department staff meetings.</li><li>Perform other related duties as assigned.</li></ul><div><br><strong>A full job description will be provided at the time of the scheduled interview.</strong></div> Sports Medicine https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3521 2026-08-20T17:00:04-04:00 2026-08-20T17:00:04-04:00 Director, Kathryn Hughes Seaber Raider Academic Center for Student-Athletes <div>Join a vibrant and purpose-driven community at <strong>Shippensburg University</strong>, located in the scenic Cumberland Valley and spread across a beautiful 210-acre campus with over 40 buildings. We offer a dynamic academic environment with 45 undergraduates, 22 graduate, and 2 doctoral programs. At Shippensburg, our mission is more than words—we are committed to inclusive collaboration, fostering a strong sense of belonging, and celebrating the achievements that drive positive change in our communities. Be part of a team that values innovation, impact, and shared success<br><br></div><div><strong>Shippensburg University offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees!</strong></div><ul><li>Effective first day of employment: low-cost medical insurance plus free dental, vision, hearing, and prescription coverage.</li><li>Choose from two generous retirement plans:<br>Alternative Retirement Plan (ARP): 5% employee contribution, 9.29% employer contribution, Immediate vesting.</li><li>State Employees’ Retirement System (SERS): 8.25% employee contribution, 2.25% employer contribution + pension calculation, 10-year vesting requirement.</li><li>Generous paid time off, employer-paid life insurance, and so much more!</li></ul><div><br>See full details in link below (for SUA employees)</div><div><a href=\"https://www.passhe.edu/hr/benefits/documents/benefit-summaries/pebtf-summary.pdf\"><strong>Full Benefits Summary (PDF)</strong></a><strong><br><br></strong>Shippensburg University seeks a collaborative, student-centered professional to serve as the <strong>Director of the Kathryn Hughes Seaber Raider (KHSR) Academic Center for Student-Athletes</strong>. The Director provides comprehensive academic support and programming for Division II student-athletes, helping them connect with the resources, services, and opportunities necessary to succeed academically and personally.</div><div><br>Reporting directly to the Executive Director of Retention, the Director works collaboratively with the Office of Student Success, Athletics, faculty, coaches, advisors, and campus partners to promote student-athlete academic success, retention, persistence, and holistic development.<br><br>The Director will also contribute to recruitment and student engagement efforts by representing the KHSR Academic Center at University events and providing prospective student-athletes and their families with clear information about academic expectations and available support. <br><br><strong>Essential Responsibilities</strong></div><ul><li>Works closely with the Office of Student Success to provide holistic support for student-athletes.</li><li>Works closely with the Director of Athletics, Associate Director of Athletics, coaching faculty, faculty advisors, and staff to support and enhance the academic success of all student-athletes.</li><li>Develops, plans, coordinates, and implements programming and initiatives designed to support student- athletes’ academic success, retention, and persistence.</li><li>Serves as the primary academic support person for all Shippensburg University Division II student-athletes.</li><li>Collaborates with the Learning Center staff to coordinate tutoring services and academic workshops for student-athletes.</li><li>Collaborate with other campus offices to arrange information-based workshops.</li><li>Provides informational presentations to prospective student-athletes and their families.</li><li>Participates in Open House, New Student Orientation, and Fall Welcome Week activities representing the Seaber RAC.</li><li>Guides student-athletes in balancing academic and athletic responsibilities while supporting their personal, academic, and career development through academic coaching, goal setting, and skill development, including study strategies, time management, informed decision-making, and understanding university academic expectations.&nbsp;</li><li>Fosters a welcoming environment that encourages student-athletes to engage with academic support services, including study halls, academic coaching, mentoring, and campus resources.</li><li>Effectively communicates with student-athletes.</li><li>Works closely with Faculty Athletics Representative and Sports Information Director on the Student-Athlete Awards Committee.&nbsp;</li><li>Ensure student-athletes understand requirements for NCAA and PSAC eligibility</li><li>Maintains accurate records and provides coaches with academic summaries and semester and annual updates on student-athletes' academic progress</li><li>Develops and implements an annual assessment plan to evaluate program effectiveness using institutional assessment and student success platforms, including Nuventive and Navigate360; analyzes assessment data and prepares reports to support continuous improvement, institutional effectiveness, and compliance.</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned or required.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Full job description will be provided at time of interview.</strong></div> Student Retention https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3529 2026-08-27T19:11:30-04:00 2026-08-27T19:11:30-04:00 Custodial Worker 1 (M-F, 6 a.m. - 2 p.m. & 3 p.m. - 11 p.m.) <div>Join a vibrant and purpose-driven community at <strong>Shippensburg University</strong>, located in the scenic Cumberland Valley and spread across a beautiful 210-acre campus with over 40 buildings. We offer a dynamic academic environment with 45 undergraduates, 22 graduate, and 2 doctoral programs. At Shippensburg, our mission is more than words—we are committed to inclusive collaboration, fostering a strong sense of belonging, and celebrating the achievements that drive positive change in our communities. Be part of a team that values innovation, impact, and shared success.<br><br>Shippensburg University offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees!<br>Effective first day of employment: low-cost medical insurance plus free dental, vision, hearing, and prescription coverage.</div><ul><li>Choose from two generous retirement plans:<ul><li>Alternative Retirement Plan (ARP): 5% employee contribution, 9.29% employer contribution, Immediate vesting.</li><li>State Employees’ Retirement System (SERS): 8.25% employee contribution, 2.25% employer contribution + pension calculation, 10-year vesting requirement.</li></ul></li><li>100% tuition waivers for you and your eligible dependents upon completion of probationary period!</li><li>Generous paid time off, employer-paid life insurance, and so much more!</li></ul><div><br>See full details in link below (for AFSCME employees)<br><strong>Full Benefits Summary (PDF)</strong><br><br>Shippensburg University is seeking several Custodial Worker 1 positions to perform a wide range of housekeeping and custodial services across campus facilities, including academic, administrative, residential, and athletic buildings. These full-time positions are scheduled Monday through Friday, with shifts from 6:00 a.m. to 2:00 p.m. and 3:00 p.m. to 11:00 p.m. The successful candidates will contribute to maintaining a clean, safe, and well-maintained environment for students, employees, and visitors.<br><br>As a member of the Facilities Divisional staff, this position is deemed essential. Essential employees must remain or report to work during partial or full day closings of the University due to hazardous road conditions, emergency circumstances or for other reasons.<br><br></div><div><strong>Key Responsibilities:<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Perform general custodial duties such as:<ul><li>Cleaning furniture, fixtures, lavatories, showers, stairways, windows, carpets, and drinking fountains</li><li>Trash removal and floor care (mopping, vacuuming)</li><li>Seasonal deep cleaning (Fall and Spring)</li></ul></li><li>Operate and inspect manual and powered custodial equipment safely</li><li>Monitor and report maintenance issues or needed repairs in buildings and furniture</li><li>Maintain supply and equipment rooms; request supplies as needed</li><li>Follow all safety protocols and participate in training programs</li><li>Provide support during emergencies and scheduled campus events</li><li>Deliver excellent customer service; respond to complaints and service needs with appropriate measure of courtesy and service.</li><li>Maintain effective verbal and written communication with supervisors and team members</li><li>Report incidents and injuries immediately to the appropriate personnel</li></ul><div><br><strong>The full job description will be provided at the time of the scheduled interview</strong></div> Custodial & Housekeeping Services https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3535 2026-08-31T16:47:47-04:00 2026-08-31T16:47:47-04:00 Violence Against Women Project Director (Temporary Grant Funded Program Coordinator 2) <div>Join a vibrant and purpose-driven community at <strong>Shippensburg University</strong>, located in the scenic Cumberland Valley and spread across a beautiful 210-acre campus with over 40 buildings. We offer a dynamic academic environment with 45 undergraduates, 22 graduate, and 2 doctoral programs. At Shippensburg, our mission is more than words—we are committed to inclusive collaboration, fostering a strong sense of belonging, and celebrating the achievements that drive positive change in our communities. Be part of a team that values innovation, impact, and shared success<br><br></div><div><strong>Shippensburg University offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees!</strong></div><ul><li>Effective first day of employment: low-cost medical insurance plus free dental, vision, hearing, and prescription coverage.</li><li>Choose from two generous retirement plans:<br>Alternative Retirement Plan (ARP): 5% employee contribution, 9.29% employer contribution, Immediate vesting.</li><li>State Employees’ Retirement System (SERS): 8.25% employee contribution, 2.25% employer contribution + pension calculation, 10-year vesting requirement.</li><li>Generous paid time off, employer-paid life insurance, and so much more!</li></ul><div><br>See full details in link below (for AFSCME employees)</div><div><a href=\"https://www.passhe.edu/hr/benefits/documents/benefit-summaries/pebtf-summary.pdf\"><strong>Full Benefits Summary (PDF)</strong></a></div><div><br>Shippensburg University is seeking for a Violence Against Women Project Director for a federally funded grant through the Department of Justice's Office of Violence Against Women (OVW). This position is temporary and grant-funded, with funding currently authorized through September 30, 2027. Grant is anticipated to extend, subject to the availability of continue funding. The purpose of the grant is to coordinate campus-wide efforts to reduce campus sexual and intimate partner violence and stalking. This position will serve as point to coordinate efforts for grant activities, policies, and protocols; generate grant reports and assessment; correspond with OVW; communicate with and schedule the internal and external Coordinated Community Response Team (CCRT); and help with budget management. <br><br><strong>Essential Duties and Responsibilities:<br></strong><br></div><div>Responsibilities include, but not limited to:</div><div>• Day-to-day operations for, oversight of, and coordination of the OVW Grant activities</div><div>• Assist with a comprehensive education program on sexual and intimate partner violence and stalking.</div><div>• Assist with coordination across internal and external service providers to increased services for survivors.</div><div>• Coordinate, communicate with, and schedule the Coordinated Community Response Team (CCRT).</div><div>• Assist with formalizing and expanding internal and external partnerships regarding sexual and intimate partner violence and stalking.</div><div>• Assist with development, management, and tracking of mandatory online first-year and transfer orientation education and prevention information.</div><div>• Assist with development, management, and tracking of population-specific violence prevention programming.</div><div>• Coordinate funder-required activities and training programs for SUPD officers, staff, student conduct and Title IX officials, and other CCRT members.</div><div>• Maintain records and track data concerning students, faculty, staff, and other participation in grant-related trainings.</div><div>• Complete required grant reports and evaluations.</div><div>• Attend OVW-required technical assistance and training meetings, travel required.</div><div>• Work with Shippensburg University financial, accounting, and grant management offices to manage grant and budget.</div><div>• Other duties as assigned</div> Dean's Office--College of Education and Human Services https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3430 2026-05-31T21:51:11-04:00 2026-06-04T10:57:37-04:00 Instructor - Global Languages & Cultures <div>The Department of Global Languages and Cultures at Shippensburg University of Pennsylvania invites applications for a full-year, three-quarter-time adjunct position<strong> </strong>specializing<strong> </strong>in<strong> </strong>German language and German culture to begin in August 2026. We seek a dynamic teacher-scholar committed to excellence in language instruction and innovative pedagogical practices.</div><div>The successful candidate will contribute to the German program by teaching 3 courses per semester at the undergraduate level. Teaching assignments may include nights and/or weekends. In addition, faculty members are expected to perform other duties as assigned in compliance with the collective bargaining agreement.<br><strong><br>Responsibilities<br></strong><br></div><div>· Teach three courses per semester, introductory through advanced courses in such areas as German language, culture, literature and/or film.</div><div>· Contribute to the assessment of the language curriculum.</div> Global Languages & Cultures https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3441 2026-06-17T13:47:31-04:00 2026-06-17T13:47:31-04:00 Instructor - English <div>The Department of English at Shippensburg University invites applications for either full-time or part-time temporary positions teaching academic writing beginning Fall 2026. Ability to teach general education literature would be considered valuable but is not required. These classes will be taught in-person, on-campus. In addition, faculty members are expected to perform other duties as assigned in compliance with the collective bargaining agreement.</div> English https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3509 2026-07-23T15:27:39-04:00 2026-07-23T15:27:40-04:00 Fiscal Technician -- Student Accounts <div>Join a vibrant and purpose-driven community at <strong>Shippensburg University</strong>, located in the scenic Cumberland Valley and spread across a beautiful 210-acre campus with over 40 buildings. We offer a dynamic academic environment with 45 undergraduate, 22 graduate, and 2 doctoral programs. At Shippensburg, our mission is more than words—we are committed to inclusive collaboration, fostering a strong sense of belonging, and celebrating the achievements that drive positive change in our communities. Be part of a team that values innovation, impact, and shared success.</div><div><br><strong>Shippensburg University offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees!</strong></div><ul><li>Effective first day of employment: low-cost medical insurance plus free dental, vision, hearing, and prescription coverage<strong>.</strong></li><li>Choose from two generous retirement plans :<ul><li>Alternative Retirement Plan (ARP):5% employee contribution, 9.29% employer contribution, Immediate vesting</li><li>State Employees’ Retirement System (SERS): 8.25% employee contribution, 2.25% employer contribution + pension calculation, 10-year vesting requirement</li></ul></li><li>100% tuition waivers for you and your eligible dependents upon completion of probationary period!</li><li>Generous paid time off, employer-paid life insurance, and so much more!</li></ul><div><br>See full details in link below (for AFSCME employees)</div><div><a href=\"https://www.passhe.edu/hr/benefits/documents/benefit-summaries/pebtf-summary.pdf\"><strong>Full Benefits Summary (PDF)</strong></a><strong><br></strong><br></div><div>Join the Student Accounts team in a key administrative and fiscal role supporting student financial operations. This position coordinates financial aid disbursements and student refunds, reviews student financial records, monitors account holds, completes reconciliations and journal entries, and helps ensure the accuracy of student accounts.</div><div><br>The successful candidate will combine strong attention to detail, independent judgment, problem-solving skills, and a commitment to providing superior customer service to students, parents, and campus constituents.<strong><br><br>This position is scheduled to work Monday through Friday from 9:30 a.m. - 6:00 p.m.</strong></div><div><strong><br>Key Responsibilities<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Receive, process, and post payments from students, parents, grantors, military sources, financial aid programs, third-party agencies, and other sources.</li><li>Process university revenue, including grants and camps/conferences, and balance cashiering activity, cash, checks, electronic payments, and credit card transactions.</li><li>Complete bank, financial aid, and university accounting system reconciliations and support audit and year-end close activities.</li><li>Review and audit accounts receivable records for accuracy and investigate discrepancies and outstanding balances.</li><li>Post and adjust student account charges, deposits, cancellations, deferments, payment plans, and approved tuition, housing, and meal waivers.</li><li>Monitor student accounts and manage enrollment, scheduling, and academic dismissal holds.</li><li>Post financial aid and process student refunds in accordance with federal, state, university, Title IV, and PASSHE policies.</li><li>Adjust student account charges and issue appropriate refunds resulting from course drops and university withdrawals.</li><li>Manage accounting entries and reconciliations for financial aid funding sources, identify discrepancies, and complete required journal entries and alternative loan fund returns.</li><li>Use Banner, TouchNet, and COGNOS reporting tools to run daily processes, analyze student accounts, and provide accurate account information.</li><li>Provide prompt, courteous customer service to students and other customers in person, by phone, and through email.</li><li>Collaborate closely with Student Accounts and Financial Aid colleagues to support a positive customer experience.</li><li>Initiate and pursue collections in accordance with University and Commonwealth policies and refer delinquent accounts to the Pennsylvania Office of Attorney General and third-party collection agencies.</li><li>Perform other related clerical accounting duties within Administration and Finance as assigned.</li></ul><div><br><strong>A full job description will be provided at the time of the scheduled interview.</strong></div> Bursar https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3515 2026-08-20T08:11:00-04:00 2026-08-20T08:11:01-04:00 Assistant Women's Basketball Coach <div>Join a vibrant and purpose-driven community at <strong>Shippensburg University</strong>, located in the scenic Cumberland Valley and spread across a beautiful 210-acre campus with over 40 buildings. We offer a dynamic academic environment with 45 undergraduate, 22 graduate, and 2 doctoral programs. At Shippensburg, our mission is more than words—we are committed to inclusive collaboration, fostering a strong sense of belonging, and celebrating the achievements that drive positive change in our communities. Be part of a team that values innovation, impact, and shared success.<br><br>This is a .25 FTE 12-month