    "https://jobs.ship.edu/postings/3536": {
      "title": "Shippensburg University Employment Opportunities | Building Automation Systems Technician 1 (3:00 p.m. - 11:00 p.m.)",
      "description": "Shippensburg University Employment Opportunities | Building Automation Systems Technician 1 (3:00 p.m. - 11:00 p.m.) Skip to Main Content About Academics Administrative Offices Admissions Athletics News and Events myShip Employment Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Useful Links Human Resources Social Equity Benefits Campus Safety & Security Building Automation Systems Technician 1 (3:00 p.m. - 11:00 p.m.) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For full consideration, all candidates must apply online at https://jobs.ship.edu with acceptance of materials continuing until the position is filled. Materials submitted in other formats including paper documents will not be considered. All applications and inquiries will remain confidential. Shippensburg University of Pennsylvania is and Equal Opportunity Employer and, in compliance with federal and state laws and university policy, is committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regards to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, or sex. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Posting Details Position Information Working Title Building Automation Systems Technician 1 (3:00 p.m. - 11:00 p.m.) Department ROC Maintenance & Operations Position Category Support Staff Posting Number SP00878 Position End Date (if other than Permanent) Hours per Week 37.5 hours per week. This position is scheduled to work from 3:00 p.m. - 11:00 p.m. Salary Range The annual salary ranges from $46,827 to $50,836, depending on experience, plus a $1.25 per-hour shift differential. The position includes a comprehensive benefits package, including tuition waivers for eligible employees and their dependents. Overtime op Full/Part Time Full Time Type of Position Permanent Position Summary Information General Description/Position Purpose Join a vibrant and purpose-driven community at Shippensburg University , located in the scenic Cumberland Valley and spread across a beautiful 210-acre campus with over 40 buildings. We offer a dynamic academic environment with 45 undergraduate, 22 graduate, and 2 doctoral programs. At Shippensburg, our mission is more than words—we are committed to inclusive collaboration, fostering a strong sense of belonging, and celebrating the achievements that drive positive change in our communities. Be part of a team that values innovation, impact, and shared success Shippensburg University offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees! Effective first day of employment: low-cost medical insurance plus free dental, vision, hearing, and prescription coverage. Choose from two generous retirement plans: Alternative Retirement Plan ( ARP ):5% employee contribution, 9.29% employer contribution, Immediate vesting. State Employees’ Retirement System ( SERS ): 8.25% employee contribution, 2.25% employer contribution + pension calculation, 10-year vesting requirement. 100% tuition waivers for you and your eligible dependents upon completion of probationary period! Generous paid time off, employer-paid life insurance, and so much more! See full details in link below (for AFSCME employees) Full Benefits Summary ( PDF ) We’re seeking a skilled Facilities Technician to support the maintenance, operation, repair, and improvement of campus buildings, systems, and infrastructure. This role performs a mix of skilled and semi-skilled work, with a focus on building automation systems ( BAS ), HVAC , plumbing, and electrical components, while addressing a wide range of facilities-related needs. As a Facilities Division Employee this position is deemed “essential” and must remain or report to work when classes are delayed or cancelled due to hazardous road or weather conditions, emergency circumstances or for other reasons as determined by operational need. This position will be working on an alternative work schedule consisting of a 10-day work cycle followed by four (4) consecutive days off. Key Duties & Responsibilities: Install, program, troubleshoot, calibrate, and maintain Building Automation Systems ( BAS ) , including sensors, actuators, control valves, VFDs, thermostats, dampers, and related controls. Monitor system performance, respond to alarms and diagnostics, commission new installations, and document software points and device connections. Support HVAC and pneumatic control systems while interpreting schematics, blueprints, wiring diagrams, and control sequences. Provide technical support and training to building occupants and staff on BAS operations. Perform multi-trade maintenance and repair work across HVAC , electrical, plumbing, carpentry, masonry, and welding disciplines. Maintain and repair building infrastructure, including pumps, piping, lighting, motors, ventilation equipment, air compressors, heating systems, doors, partitions, furniture, electrical fixtures, and circuits. Conduct preventive maintenance, facility inspections, and corrective repairs to ensure safe and reliable operation of campus facilities. Utilize a computerized maintenance management system ( CMMS ) to manage work orders, document labor and materials, and track maintenance activities. Maintain inventory, identify and report unsafe conditions, and recommend equipment replacement or system improvements. Participate in emergency response activities, after-hours call coverage, lock changes, and snow/ice removal operations. Support campus events through facility setup, teardown, and troubleshooting. Obtain Pennsylvania Pesticide Applicator Certification in Swimming Pool Management (Category 24) within 180 days of hire. Qualifications: Proficiency in at least two trades: plumbing, electrical, HVAC , carpentry, or mechanical systems Working knowledge of BAS software and commercial system components Ability to diagnose and resolve mechanical/electrical issues using tools and technical documentation Familiarity with safety standards, CMMS , and Microsoft Office Strong communication skills and teamwork mindset Must obtain PA Pesticide Applicator Certification (Category 24 – Swimming Pool Management) within 180 days of hire A full job description will be provided at the time of the scheduled interview. Minimum Qualifications Three Years of experience in the maintenance, repair, or installation of HVAC equipment, related to digitally controlled equipment, or Building Automation (BA) Systems which includes at least one year working with industrial or commercial electronic controls and sensors. OR An equivalent combination of experience and training which includes at least one year working with industrial or commercial electronic controls or sensors. Special Requirements: Possession of an active Pennsylvania non-commercial Class C Driver’s license or equivalent. Preferred Qualifications Successful completion of the HVAC and Building Automation Technician Trainee Program. Posting Detail Information Open Date 09/02/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions Summary For full consideration, all candidates must apply online at https://jobs.ship.edu with acceptance of materials continuing until the position is filled. Materials submitted in other formats including paper documents will not be considered. All applications and inquiries will remain confidential. Shippensburg University of Pennsylvania is and Equal Opportunity Employer and, in compliance with federal and state laws and university policy, is committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regards to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, or sex. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Additional Information All Shippensburg University employees are expected to demonstrate an understanding of and commitment to the University’s core values of teamwork and collaboration, dependability, initiative, problem solving, and clear communication. University employees are expected to demonstrate good interpersonal and communication skills with all members of the campus community. They will strive to maintain integrity, effectiveness and efficiency by upholding customer service throughout all levels of performance. All university employees are required to comply with university policies, state and federal laws/statutes prohibiting any type of Discrimination, Harassment or Retaliation. Safeguarding confidential, personal data and/or records of employees, students, customers and other related constituents is the responsibility of all University employees. It is the duty of all members of the University community to take part in the maintenance of a safe campus. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current employee of Shippensburg University? Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Employer website Indeed CareerLink HigherEd Jobs LinkedIn Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral * Did you successfully complete the HVAC and Building Automation Technician Trainee program? Yes No * Do you have three years of experience in in the maintenance, repair or installation of HVAC equipment, related to digitally controlled equipment, or Building Automation (BA) Systems which includes one year of working with industrial or commercial electronic controls and sensors? Yes No * Do you have an active Pennsylvania non-commercial Class C Driver's license or equivalent? Yes No * What interests you about working at Shippensburg University? Benefits Salary Tuition Waiver Working in Higher Education Closer To Home Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume List of References Optional Documents This page is an official publication of Shippensburg University: A member of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education . Shippensburg University - 1871 Old Main Drive - Shippensburg, PA 17257 - (717) 477-7447 Ask a Question/Provide Feedback | Privacy Statement | View on Mobile To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
